WEBVTT

00:10.780 --> 00:14.360
I'm glad you two could make it.
Brald filled me in.

00:15.030 --> 00:18.300
You already know Lucas and Elijah, right?

00:18.300 --> 00:19.080
Yeah.

00:19.870 --> 00:24.210
The name's Reginald Bastion. 
I'm an A-rank Augmenter.

00:24.530 --> 00:29.450
I'm Kriol Masser.  
I'm also an A-rank Augmenter.

00:29.880 --> 00:32.660
Water's my element. Nice to meet you.

00:33.130 --> 00:35.890
I am Oliver Hemmbet.

00:36.240 --> 00:38.190
I'm an A-rank Conjurer.

00:39.880 --> 00:43.770
<i>That stone... He said his name was Oliver?</i>

00:44.570 --> 00:48.220
<i>He's an Emitter like Alice.</i>

00:49.480 --> 00:52.180
<i>Having one in the party 
will come in handy.</i>

00:52.840 --> 00:54.320
I'm Samantha.

00:54.900 --> 00:58.570
I'm an A-rank Conjurer.
Pleased to be working with you all.

00:59.180 --> 01:01.480
How about you, masked man?

01:01.480 --> 01:04.830
I'm Note. I'm an A-rank Augmenter.

01:05.220 --> 01:08.390
My name's Jasmine. 
I'm an AA-rank Augmenter.

01:08.990 --> 01:12.410
It's a relief having another 
AA-rank in the party.

01:13.180 --> 01:15.590
Well, I see everyone's here.

01:15.900 --> 01:17.250
And you're late!

01:18.210 --> 01:19.710
I guess I am.

01:20.380 --> 01:24.360
You're all aware of this, but I'll be 
the party's leader, Brald Ladon.

01:24.790 --> 01:27.600
I'm a newly AA-ranked Augmenter.

01:28.530 --> 01:33.290
Those bags... Do the two of 
you not have dimension rings?

01:33.290 --> 01:34.020
Right.

01:36.550 --> 01:39.320
I'd store their stuff with mine,

01:39.320 --> 01:42.620
but I've already got Samantha's,
so I'm out of space.

01:42.920 --> 01:45.120
I can store their bags in mine.

01:45.420 --> 01:46.970
I should have room to spare.

01:48.730 --> 01:49.770
Is that all?

01:49.770 --> 01:51.780
Yeah, that's everything.

01:51.780 --> 01:52.830
We appreciate it.

01:53.260 --> 01:54.460
Thank you.

01:54.460 --> 01:55.900
Oh, it's fine.

01:56.440 --> 01:57.470
Now, then...

01:58.070 --> 01:59.980
Let's get underway.

03:32.980 --> 03:38.000
#5 The King's Struggles.

03:33.870 --> 03:37.540
<i>We're in this cave, teamed 
up with complete strangers,</i>

03:37.540 --> 03:39.510
<i>because of Brald's invitation.</i>

03:40.340 --> 03:43.950
There's supposed to be a massive 
magic stone at the lowest layer.

03:43.950 --> 03:45.060
A magic stone?

03:45.490 --> 03:47.680
It's a natural rock formation that can act

03:47.680 --> 03:51.490
as an amplifier for mana as well
 as a versatile power source.

03:52.040 --> 03:55.250
I was hired by someone to retrieve it,

03:55.250 --> 03:58.060
which is why I'm assembling a 
team of skilled adventurers.

04:00.510 --> 04:02.820
You know Lucas and Elijah, right?

04:03.370 --> 04:04.260
Yes.

04:04.570 --> 04:09.320
They're going to be joining me, and 
they recommended you and Jasmine.

04:11.110 --> 04:16.770
<i>With Jasmine, Elijah, and Lucas all 
participating, I decided I may as well.</i>

04:17.470 --> 04:20.780
<i>In part, to make sure 
nothing happens to them.</i>

04:21.320 --> 04:25.020
What's got you folks participating 
in this dungeon raid, anyway?

04:25.950 --> 04:30.290
Well, Brald said he was 
gathering talented A-ranks.

04:32.190 --> 04:33.790
Then you don't care about the reward?

04:34.120 --> 04:38.290
I mean, it's not as if 
I'm lacking in money.

04:38.290 --> 04:40.740
Same here. I'm less 
interested in the reward

04:40.740 --> 04:44.790
and more in the credit from 
taking down an imposing dungeon.

04:44.790 --> 04:47.800
Well, it must be nice not to 
have to worry about money.

04:48.410 --> 04:51.770
I've got a bunch of kids, 
so I can never have enough.

04:51.770 --> 04:56.560
Likewise. I wanna open a bakery,
 and that's gonna take a big investment.

04:56.800 --> 05:00.840
Our motives may be distinct, 
but we're all in the same party.

05:00.840 --> 05:02.570
Let's work together!

05:03.480 --> 05:04.360
He said it.

05:05.900 --> 05:07.410
Here's the entrance.

05:08.600 --> 05:10.580
Let's move in.

05:13.670 --> 05:16.730
<i>This dungeon seems ordinary enough.</i>

05:18.220 --> 05:20.840
I've scouted ahead already.

05:20.840 --> 05:24.350
Now that's a leader for you! Good to know.

05:24.350 --> 05:28.090
Does that mean you know the path 
to the lowest floor already?

05:28.580 --> 05:31.100
No, I didn't get that far in.

05:31.340 --> 05:34.100
But this path should take 
us in the right direction.

05:34.390 --> 05:36.440
Seems easy enough!

05:38.090 --> 05:42.490
Not exactly. The creatures in 
here are said to be immortal.

05:42.490 --> 05:45.360
Even if they're slain, 
they come back to life.

05:45.640 --> 05:47.790
Is that really possible?

05:47.790 --> 05:51.100
Not only that, but there's no 
collecting mana cores down here.

05:51.100 --> 05:53.510
So there's no real upside to combat.

05:53.510 --> 05:55.620
That's why it's called the Tomb of Terror.

05:56.010 --> 05:57.450
What's up with that?

05:57.450 --> 06:00.130
That's why I want us to tackle 
battle as efficiently as possible.

06:00.510 --> 06:02.390
Conserve as much mana as you can.

06:03.210 --> 06:05.380
Does killing them with a single 
spell sound efficient enough?

06:05.610 --> 06:08.850
Easy there. Let's leave it at that.

06:08.850 --> 06:09.640
What are you on about?

06:10.170 --> 06:12.640
I mean, the other day 
you overdid it, and...

06:17.080 --> 06:18.960
Oh, I remember that.

06:18.960 --> 06:19.800
See?

06:19.800 --> 06:20.940
Shut up!

06:23.750 --> 06:25.290
It's awfully quiet.

06:25.620 --> 06:28.450
There shouldn't be any 
monsters in this area.

06:28.920 --> 06:31.620
Seriously? How dull.

06:31.620 --> 06:33.450
I wouldn't let my guard 
down if I were you.

06:34.740 --> 06:38.190
There's never any strong monsters 
near the entrance, anyway.

06:38.710 --> 06:39.800
<i>Good grief.</i>

06:41.220 --> 06:43.080
<i>You never learn, do you, boy?</i>

06:48.550 --> 06:49.720
Bat Runners!

06:51.330 --> 06:53.000
There's so many.

06:55.930 --> 06:56.790
Get down!

07:12.930 --> 07:14.990
Save your stamina and mana!

07:14.990 --> 07:16.490
Easier said than done!

07:16.770 --> 07:19.500
Were there this many when 
you came by earlier?!

07:19.500 --> 07:20.600
No.

07:21.100 --> 07:22.490
<i>This is getting us nowhere.</i>

07:23.480 --> 07:24.940
Lucas, take care of it!

07:27.190 --> 07:28.280
I'll back you up!

07:40.020 --> 07:41.260
Got them!

07:41.260 --> 07:43.890
Great work. But you went overboard.

07:45.970 --> 07:48.610
I just said to conserve mana!

07:48.610 --> 07:51.030
What's it matter if I got them?!

07:55.240 --> 07:58.010
We need to hurry before 
they finish reviving.

08:08.440 --> 08:12.050
Elijah, can you make a 
stairway on the wall?

08:23.570 --> 08:25.310
Good. Come on.

08:27.620 --> 08:31.060
You all right? I'll go on ahead.

08:31.430 --> 08:34.320
That way I can catch you if you fall.

08:34.320 --> 08:37.820
I appreciate it. 
I'm terrible with heights.

08:38.730 --> 08:42.830
There should be a passageway 
to the lowest level further in.

08:42.830 --> 08:43.990
There "should be"?

08:44.900 --> 08:47.540
Well... it was there 
when I came by earlier.

08:47.540 --> 08:49.780
Either way, let's get going.

08:49.780 --> 08:52.050
The sooner we grab that 
treasure, the better, right?

08:53.140 --> 08:54.570
You've got a point.

08:56.340 --> 08:58.800
My magic saved us all, didn't it?

09:00.190 --> 09:02.060
You were a big help.

09:02.450 --> 09:06.060
Note. I advise against 
wasting your mana.

09:06.360 --> 09:07.910
You worry too much.

09:24.060 --> 09:25.020
Traps?

09:25.590 --> 09:26.790
Hey!

09:27.110 --> 09:29.080
You didn't mention any traps!

09:31.870 --> 09:33.880
<i>It wasn't supposed to be like this.</i>

09:35.940 --> 09:41.420
If you find some skilled adventurers 
to go with you, I'll pay extra.

09:41.420 --> 09:44.060
Right. I've got a few in mind.

09:44.460 --> 09:47.390
That sounds promising.

09:47.390 --> 09:51.320
What exactly is this Tomb of Terror 
dungeon supposed to be like?

09:51.570 --> 09:54.810
There are no traps, 
and no monsters of note.

09:55.190 --> 09:58.250
The name stems from how the 
inhabitants are immortal.

09:58.600 --> 10:01.810
You'll need adventurers skilled 
enough to incapacitate them,

10:01.810 --> 10:04.830
even if they can't kill them.

10:05.660 --> 10:09.850
I'm sure the group you have in 
mind should be able to handle it.

10:10.700 --> 10:11.890
I think so.

10:15.620 --> 10:18.100
This map will show you the 
way to the lowest layer.

10:19.190 --> 10:23.060
<i>He said there were no traps! 
What's going on here?!</i>

10:27.910 --> 10:30.390
Let's be cautious as we proceed, everyone.

10:34.740 --> 10:36.900
Is anyone else hot?

10:36.900 --> 10:38.110
It's just you.

10:38.430 --> 10:41.110
I'm feeling kinda hot, too.

10:41.110 --> 10:42.920
Something strange is going on.

10:42.920 --> 10:46.370
You mean it wasn't this hot 
when you came here before?

10:46.650 --> 10:49.870
That's not what I mean.

10:50.130 --> 10:54.900
<i>They're probably feeling the intense 
pressure coming from the opposite direction.</i>

11:04.130 --> 11:05.720
What is this place?

11:05.720 --> 11:08.750
Yeah. And why's it so hot?

11:10.810 --> 11:11.770
What's going on?!

11:11.770 --> 11:13.100
I don't know, either!

11:13.100 --> 11:14.590
All I've been hearing from 
you is "I don't know"

11:14.590 --> 11:16.270
and "that's weird" for a while now!

11:16.270 --> 11:18.990
Did you scout this place or not?!

11:21.460 --> 11:22.740
You bastard!

11:24.950 --> 11:25.900
Kriol!

11:27.740 --> 11:28.860
I've got it!

11:40.150 --> 11:42.130
Just tell us the truth already!

11:42.420 --> 11:45.960
Did you check this place out or not?!

11:46.500 --> 11:51.640
The client gave me the details of 
the dungeon and showed me a map.

11:52.570 --> 11:55.270
I knew about the Bat Runners, but...

11:55.270 --> 11:59.550
Then the traps? And the huge worm?

12:00.670 --> 12:01.980
Those...

12:03.620 --> 12:06.780
In other words, we ran into a mana beast 
that wasn't supposed to be here.

12:08.790 --> 12:12.270
Since when do new kinds of mana 
beasts appear for the first time

12:12.270 --> 12:13.290
inside a dungeon?!

12:14.040 --> 12:16.190
<i>Unless it didn't suddenly appear,</i>

12:16.190 --> 12:18.550
<i>and was here all along,
and he was lied to.</i>

12:19.320 --> 12:21.190
<i>But to what end?</i>

12:29.580 --> 12:31.270
Follow me.

12:32.040 --> 12:33.970
Brald is lying.

12:33.970 --> 12:37.610
If we follow his lead, we'll be 
prey for monsters sooner or later.

12:38.680 --> 12:43.200
We'll seize the treasure while 
they're busy with the worm!

12:43.200 --> 12:44.380
But...

12:44.380 --> 12:45.970
Come on, let's just go!

12:49.850 --> 12:51.700
<i>Something strange is going on.</i>

12:51.700 --> 12:52.810
Wait!

12:52.810 --> 12:55.520
I'm not going to die here 
with the rest of you!

12:55.520 --> 12:56.210
Don't go!

12:56.590 --> 12:57.290
Lucas!

12:57.290 --> 12:58.460
I know!

13:08.230 --> 13:09.720
Oliver, get inside!

13:11.150 --> 13:12.600
What are you talking about?!

13:13.060 --> 13:16.150
Didn't you hear?! I'm not going to die—

13:41.780 --> 13:42.690
Samantha.

13:44.760 --> 13:49.740
Exchange that gem with the one in your 
staff. It'll be more powerful.

13:54.470 --> 13:55.640
We need to get out of here.

13:55.860 --> 14:01.650
Y-Yeah. Note is right, we need to get 
clear before there's another eruption.

14:09.500 --> 14:11.700
Kriol! Do it!

14:11.700 --> 14:12.920
It's done!

14:17.990 --> 14:18.890
Damn it!

14:18.890 --> 14:22.230
Samantha! Elijah! Attack!

14:31.510 --> 14:35.430
Oliver's stone really is powerful.

14:44.390 --> 14:46.190
Are we lacking in firepower?

14:47.780 --> 14:51.070
Jasmine! Reginald! Move with me!

14:55.780 --> 14:58.720
Jasmine! You and I will distract it!

14:58.720 --> 14:59.580
Understood.

14:59.580 --> 15:03.090
While we do, Reginald will nail its head!

15:03.090 --> 15:04.340
Got it!

15:04.810 --> 15:07.590
Lucas, Note, see if you 
can find a weakness!

15:07.590 --> 15:08.580
Right.

15:14.380 --> 15:16.850
<i>If normal fire magic 
isn't having an effect,</i>

15:16.850 --> 15:20.850
<i>then maybe something with 
a higher temperature will.</i>

15:38.150 --> 15:39.000
Note!

15:57.070 --> 16:00.330
I'm not chickening out... am I?

16:00.790 --> 16:01.770
Lucas!

16:04.140 --> 16:05.020
Jasmine!

16:13.580 --> 16:14.530
Lucas!

16:21.180 --> 16:23.420
Damn thing got away.

16:23.420 --> 16:26.040
Still, we should be safe for a while.

16:26.700 --> 16:28.310
Let's move while we've got the chance.

16:32.520 --> 16:35.550
<i>The worm wasn't trying to kill us.</i>

16:35.830 --> 16:38.750
<i>It was trying to buy time 
until the next eruption.</i>

16:40.100 --> 16:41.710
Lucas, we need the barrier—

16:43.730 --> 16:44.810
Idiot!

17:04.530 --> 17:05.610
Note...

17:06.430 --> 17:07.940
I'm glad you're okay.

17:07.940 --> 17:09.090
You mean that?

17:10.430 --> 17:12.340
I didn't ask for your help.

17:15.730 --> 17:16.890
Are you all right?

17:16.890 --> 17:19.350
Yeah. What about you, Brald?

17:19.770 --> 17:21.100
Are you hurt?

17:23.050 --> 17:24.850
Oh, no—

17:25.830 --> 17:28.650
We need to hurry and get out of here.

17:32.430 --> 17:33.280
Hang in there.

17:33.280 --> 17:34.350
We're almost done.

17:44.250 --> 17:46.120
Care for something to eat?

17:46.980 --> 17:47.970
Thanks.

17:48.670 --> 17:51.630
My trademark sandwich. Always bring 
them with me when I'm traveling.

17:52.590 --> 17:54.360
Pretty good, right?

17:54.900 --> 17:55.880
Very.

17:56.390 --> 17:58.010
It's Clara's recipe.

17:58.010 --> 17:58.890
Clara?

17:59.290 --> 18:00.770
My fiancée.

18:01.500 --> 18:05.890
Then what you said about a bakery... 
you'd be running it with her?

18:08.410 --> 18:09.650
Well, yeah.

18:09.650 --> 18:13.020
Let her know that her recipe is amazing.

18:13.020 --> 18:15.840
Sure. She'll be glad to hear it.

18:15.840 --> 18:16.900
Knock it off!

18:17.140 --> 18:19.130
I'm not wrong!

18:19.130 --> 18:21.540
I only agreed to this 
quest because I heard

18:21.540 --> 18:24.790
the leader was a veteran 
AA-rank Augmenter!

18:24.790 --> 18:30.170
But look what's happened! Our Emitter 
is gone, and you're missing an arm!

18:30.600 --> 18:32.460
What are we supposed to do now?!

18:32.460 --> 18:36.670
You act like you didn't drop your weapon! 
You were helpless when we needed you!

18:37.190 --> 18:39.930
Note was the one who saved you!
 Where do you get off?!

18:39.930 --> 18:41.160
Shut your mouth!

18:41.160 --> 18:42.930
I said knock it off!

18:43.270 --> 18:47.680
If you'd been able to cast that 
barrier, I'd still have my arm!

18:47.900 --> 18:49.790
Don't blame it on me!

18:49.790 --> 18:50.820
Lucas.

18:52.190 --> 18:53.470
That's enough.

18:53.930 --> 18:55.070
What do you want?!

18:55.070 --> 18:57.570
There's no point in criticizing 
other's mistakes.

19:02.650 --> 19:07.120
Brald. Before we continue,
I want you to make a decision.

19:07.580 --> 19:10.850
Are we still pursuing the treasure? 
Or are we going to give up?

19:12.280 --> 19:14.880
And no more secrets.

19:15.560 --> 19:18.380
That kind of anxiety can 
spell disaster in a dungeon.

19:20.570 --> 19:23.390
I lied about scouting the 
dungeon ahead of time.

19:24.350 --> 19:26.990
I only know what the client told me.

19:26.990 --> 19:29.020
I never set foot in here.

19:32.850 --> 19:34.420
<i>I thought as much.</i>

19:35.030 --> 19:37.780
I'm not going to say 
that I paid the price

19:38.300 --> 19:40.150
for putting you all in danger, but...

19:40.700 --> 19:43.660
But I don't want to give up.

19:44.300 --> 19:48.410
This is likely to be the 
last dungeon I set foot in.

19:48.820 --> 19:51.160
So, please... let's keep going.

19:51.480 --> 19:53.650
We should give up on the quest.

19:53.650 --> 19:57.670
Jasmine's right! You can't keep 
going with those injuries!

19:57.980 --> 20:00.770
Even missing an arm, I'm 
a AA-rank Augmenter.

20:01.700 --> 20:03.950
I won't slow the rest of you down.

20:05.380 --> 20:09.280
As things stand, it's not gonna 
be any easier turning back.

20:09.280 --> 20:12.390
That magic stone had better 
actually be down here.

20:12.390 --> 20:14.580
That I'm certain of.

20:16.500 --> 20:17.320
Please!

20:18.110 --> 20:21.030
<i>We're in for hell no matter 
what choice we make.</i>

20:21.820 --> 20:23.090
<i>In that case...</i>

20:23.930 --> 20:25.100
Fine.

20:25.100 --> 20:26.130
Note?

20:30.430 --> 20:35.340
And given that we're moving ahead 
I think that Note should act as leader.

20:36.550 --> 20:38.840
You had the calmest,

20:38.840 --> 20:42.970
most effective response to 
unforeseen trouble of anyone here.

20:43.220 --> 20:45.090
You're a natural-born leader.

20:46.330 --> 20:47.110
What do you say?

20:51.010 --> 20:51.880
All right.

20:56.040 --> 21:00.270
I was told that the path to the 
lowest level is beyond this door.

21:14.030 --> 21:15.140
What the...
